            %a{:href => "#Selinger05"}> Selinger 05
            ) … see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#CoeckeHeunen11"}> Coecke-Heunen 11, section 2
            ) for a quick summary …
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#universal_property Universal property
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are indexed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,m, \cdots
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are quantum operations from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ×
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \times m
            matrices is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal category
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal structure
            given by multiplication of numbers. Being semicartesian, the monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            (the number
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            In fact, this category has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the semicartesian reflection of the monoidal category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are isometries between them, where an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\to n
            is an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\times n
            complex matrix
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi V
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V V* = I
          %p
            In detail, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            says that for any strict semicartesian monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            and any monoidal functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Isometries
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Isometries}\to \mathcal{D}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Isometries
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mi Quantum
                            %mi Channels
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  {Isometries} &amp;\rightarrow&amp; {Quantum Channels} \\
                  \&amp;\searrow&amp;\downarrow\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathcal{D}
                  }
          %p This fits a physical intuition as follows. Suppose that the isometries are a model of reality, as in the many worlds interpretation and the Church of the larger Hilbert space. But in practice the observer cannot access the entirety of reality, and so some bits are hidden. The canonical way to model this hiding is to do it freely, which is to form the semicartesian reflection.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#unitary_quantum_channels Unitary quantum channels
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+quantum+channel"} unitary quantum channel
            is a quantum channel whose restriction to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+states"} pure states
            acts by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+transformation"} unitary transformation
            just as a loss-less
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gate"} quantum gate
            does.
          %p
            Concretely, in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#InTermsOfKrausDecompositions"} operator-sym decomposition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
